cdk.out/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Written by the CDK CLI on any `synth`/`deploy`, and it must not be committed: it caches
# context lookups keyed by *account and region*, so the file that lands names whichever
# account happened to run the command. Committing it pins every later checkout's lookups to
# that account -- and pins them stale, which is worse than not caching, because a stale entry
# is used in preference to asking. `make deploy` already keeps its own outputs file out of the
# tree for the same reason; this is the one the CDK CLI writes behind it.
infra/cdk.context.json

# The remote coding agent's own working directory, and the name it quarantines a
# repository-provided one to. `.agent/` is where a run's own specification, review and
# memory live, and `nodes/checkout.py::_quarantine_repo_agent_dir` renames a
# clone-provided `.agent/` to `.agent.repo/` so repository content is not read as this
# task's specification and memory. Both are per-run scratch, so neither belongs in a
# commit -- and a committed `.agent.repo/` would additionally make that function's
# already-moved guard (`destination.exists()`) true before anything had been moved,
# leaving a repository's own `.agent/` in place to be read as this task's state.
.agent/
.agent.repo/
